1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,545
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:06,089
‪["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,719
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,929
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:15,974
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,226
[Olga] <i>But you know,</i>
<i>in fairness to Ibyang,</i>

7
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:20,729
<i>she's such a sweet and thoughtful child.</i>

8
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:23,982
Whoever her parents are,
they're very lucky.

9
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:26,234
I think it's time
you give the child back to us.

10
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:29,154
Why? Are you returning her
to her real mother?

11
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:30,238
[in English] That's none of your concern.

12
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:32,323
[Mayor's wife] <i>They picked up a man.</i>

13
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:34,534
They say he's good at fighting.

14
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:37,287
- [in English] You will…
- [grunts]

15
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:39,873
[in English] You're not going to say
where the laptop is.

16
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:43,501
[in English] Right now, I'm searching
for all of your beloved.

17
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:48,256
[in English] And I will kill every
one of them right in front of your face.

18
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:49,632
[in English] Mission status.

19
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,469
[in English] Outside the establishment.

20
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:56,431
[in English] Potential headquarters
of Anthony "Atoy" Padua.

21
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:58,099
[Samir, in English]
Is she important to you?

22
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,934
[in English] Does she matter to you?

23
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:01,811
[Atoy, in English] No, no, no! Stop! Stop!

24
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,897
[in English] I'm the only one
who can access it,

25
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:07,192
and I can erase every classified info
you have on there.

26
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:08,860
[in English] Plan didn't work out, huh?

27
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,820
[cackles]

28
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:12,572
[groans]

29
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:13,490
[moans]

30
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:14,991
PREVIOUSLY

31
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:18,745
So, if you want to live longer,
learn to listen to me.

32
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:21,206
- [Red, in English] You understand? Huh?
- [moaning]

33
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:23,541
[Janine] <i>Uncle Red locked me and Mommy up.</i>

34
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:25,752
What did you do to Audrey,
to my granddaughter?!

35
00:01:26,252 --> 00:01:27,170
[Red] <i>She's not really your granddaughter.</i>

36
00:01:28,546 --> 00:01:29,631
<i>She's not really Audrey's daughter either.</i>

37
00:01:29,714 --> 00:01:31,382
You're truly worthless.

38
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:34,427
[grunts and groans]

39
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:37,222
[Red] <i>She was going to report us</i>
<i>to the police!</i>

40
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:38,848
<i>I just stopped her!</i>

41
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:41,810
[Atoy] You think you're tough
for beating up a tied-up man?

42
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:43,728
[Samir, in English] <i>Stand up</i>
<i>and let us fight.</i>

43
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:44,813
[Atoy grunts]

44
00:01:45,396 --> 00:01:49,818
[music fades]

45
00:01:57,909 --> 00:01:59,536
[rousing music playing]

46
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:01,746
[gasps]

47
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:06,543
[gasps]

48
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:11,297
[gun cocks]

49
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:42,745
[music fades]

50
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:45,582
[in English] Kill me now. Huh?

51
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:47,292
[in English] Kill me now!

52
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:49,294
[in English] What, huh?!

53
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:50,879
This is what you want, isn't it?!

54
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:51,796
This will make you happy, won't it?!

55
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:52,714
[in English] Kill me now!

56
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:54,424
- [grunts]
- [in English] Do it!

57
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:56,384
- [growls]
- [in English] Do it!

58
00:02:56,467 --> 00:02:58,052
[tense music playing]

59
00:02:58,136 --> 00:03:00,221
[heavy breathing]

60
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:02,724
[in English] You're not worth it.

61
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:06,936
[in English] You're not… worth it.

62
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:07,854
‪[heavy breathing]

63
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,070
[in English, softly] Not worth it?

64
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:18,615
You're the one who will die!

65
00:03:22,327 --> 00:03:23,369
[Red grunts]

66
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:27,415
[groans]

67
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:32,253
Find him.

68
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,005
When you see him, shoot him.

69
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:36,007
Boss, are you sure? He's your father.

70
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:38,509
- It's none of your business! Hurry up!
- [thug] Yes.

71
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:42,472
[suave theme music playing]

72
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:10,833
[music fades]

73
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:17,465
- [Gavin] Janine? Janine!
- [car door clicks shut]

74
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:20,134
- Brother Gavin! [sobs]
- [Gavin] Why are you crying?

75
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:22,011
- [in English] What's wrong?
- They're--

76
00:04:22,095 --> 00:04:23,554
Grandpa and Uncle Red are fighting!

77
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:26,349
Uncle Red is bad.
He locked me and Mommy up!

78
00:04:26,432 --> 00:04:27,558
- [in English] What?
- [sobs]

79
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:29,185
Huh?

80
00:04:30,019 --> 00:04:33,898
- [gunfire blasting in the distance]
- [gasping]

81
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:35,775
[tense music playing]

82
00:04:38,736 --> 00:04:42,657
- [music fades]
- [panting and groaning]

83
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,541
[in English] Dad!

84
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:52,917
[somber music playing]

85
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:54,877
[stammers, in English] Dad!

86
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:56,963
- [gasping]
- [groaning]

87
00:04:57,046 --> 00:04:58,923
What happened, Dad, huh?

88
00:04:59,424 --> 00:05:01,384
- Who-- Who did this to you?
- [groans]

89
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:04,929
It was Red. Red did this to me.

90
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:08,266
- He's ruthless.
- [groans]

91
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:09,684
You need to be taken to the hospital.

92
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:10,810
- [grunts]
- [shrieks]

93
00:05:10,893 --> 00:05:13,688
[in English] Dad! Dad! Dad!

94
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:14,897
‪[groans]

95
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:16,107
Run away.

96
00:05:16,899 --> 00:05:18,526
- Audrey, run away!
- [in English] No!

97
00:05:18,609 --> 00:05:20,737
[in English] I'm not leaving
you and my daughter, Dad!

98
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,780
[in English] No, no!

99
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:23,906
- [sobs]
- [groans]

100
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:25,199
[in English] No, Dad.

101
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:30,496
Forgive me, my child,
if I didn't tell you the truth.

102
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:36,044
And I'm sorry you grew up
in this kind of life.

103
00:05:37,086 --> 00:05:38,004
[in English] I'm sorry.

104
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:40,423
Dad, that doesn't matter now. [sobs]

105
00:05:40,506 --> 00:05:42,550
[in English] We have to get out of here.

106
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:45,720
Stand up, Dad. Get up.

107
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:49,140
- Please, get up!
- [groans]

108
00:05:49,223 --> 00:05:50,725
[sobs]

109
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:54,353
We can still escape!

110
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:56,731
[in English] Dad, come on!
I just have to find Janine!

111
00:05:57,482 --> 00:05:58,941
I already helped her escape.

112
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:03,696
But there's something
you need to know about Janine.

113
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,822
[heavy breathing]

114
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:06,532
She's not really your daughter.

115
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:11,245
[music fades]

116
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:13,039
[pensive music playing]

117
00:06:13,122 --> 00:06:15,917
[pants, in English] No. That's…

118
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:19,378
[in English] Tha-Th-That's impossible,
Dad.

119
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:26,803
Red and Martina… They lied about Janine.

120
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:29,764
They deceived us.

121
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:34,352
They deceived us. [groans]

122
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:36,813
[in English] We'll-- We'll--
We'll figure it out later, Dad.

123
00:06:36,896 --> 00:06:39,107
We need to get out of here.

124
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,358
- Please try!
- [groans]

125
00:06:40,441 --> 00:06:42,777
- [in English] Help me. Please try, Dad.
- [groans]

126
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:45,446
[in English] Dad!

127
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:47,115
[music fades]

128
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:49,826
[metal clanging in the distance]

129
00:06:49,909 --> 00:06:52,078
[suspicious music playing]

130
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:03,172
[in English] Let's go, coward.

131
00:07:03,256 --> 00:07:04,549
[in English] I'll let you hit me first.

132
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:06,717
[in English] You need this one. Okay?

133
00:07:07,301 --> 00:07:08,302
Boss. Boss is going to fight.

134
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:11,347
Boss, you can do it.

135
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:12,432
You can do it, boss!

136
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,227
[in English] Resting for focus. Focus!

137
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:17,186
[in English] I'm right here!

138
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,271
[grunts]

139
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:19,981
[grunts]

140
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:22,733
- [thug mutters]
- [in English] Okay…

141
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:24,110
Boss, you can do it, boss!

142
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:26,446
[in English] I see. You're ready, huh.

143
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,531
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

144
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:29,991
[chuckles]

145
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:32,994
[grunting and groaning]

146
00:07:33,077 --> 00:07:34,162
[grunts]

147
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:39,000
[in English] Let's do this!

148
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,002
[Samir, in English] Okay.

149
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:43,421
[in English] Okay.

150
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:50,845
[grunting and groaning]

151
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:01,314
[music fades]

152
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:04,150
[tense music playing]

153
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:07,987
[groans]

154
00:08:24,795 --> 00:08:27,423
[grunting and groaning]

155
00:08:31,969 --> 00:08:35,556
[grunting and groaning]

156
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:38,976
- [ominous music playing]
- [buzzing]

157
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:42,855
[groaning]

158
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:55,117
[Lily sobbing]

159
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,786
[in English] Get the cutter.

160
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:59,622
[Lily, in English] No, no, no, no.

161
00:09:00,831 --> 00:09:02,833
[in English] No, no, no, no, no!

162
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:05,795
[in English] No! Brother, don't.

163
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:07,547
Brother, brother, don't, don't, brother!

164
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:10,007
- [sobs] Don't!
- [Atoy] You're unfair!

165
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:12,635
But I won't back down. What, round two?!

166
00:09:13,135 --> 00:09:16,013
- [Lily] Don't!
- [Atoy] What's that?

167
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:17,515
Hey! Don't, don't, don't, don't,
don't, don't!

168
00:09:17,598 --> 00:09:18,516
- Don't, don't!
- [Lily screams]

169
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:21,435
- [guttural cry of pain]
- [buzzing]

170
00:09:29,527 --> 00:09:30,736
You demons!

171
00:09:31,862 --> 00:09:35,074
[bawling]

172
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:39,203
- [Lily screaming]
- [guttural cry of pain]

173
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:49,338
[heavy breathing]

174
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:55,303
Mmm, there. Let me see.

175
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,221
Ah, that looks good!

176
00:10:00,516 --> 00:10:03,185
Ma, where are we going?

177
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:04,437
Just nearby.

178
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,859
Can we take a picture first?

179
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:11,235
Oh, sure.

180
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:13,070
[somber music playing]

181
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:14,655
[camera shutter snaps]

182
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:17,283
- One more.
- Ah, one more.

183
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,410
[camera shutter snaps]

184
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:22,496
- Ma.
- Mmm?

185
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:26,250
Is it okay if you go to school?

186
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:28,669
[melancholic music playing]

187
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:32,173
Because Tatoy might not be there yet.

188
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,885
Um… Why… Why is that?

189
00:10:36,802 --> 00:10:37,845
What's happening?

190
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:42,642
Because our moving-up ceremony is near.

191
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:47,855
I'm the top student,
and they said there's a medal!

192
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:49,565
Wow.

193
00:10:50,566 --> 00:10:55,071
Um, can you be the one to put it on me?

194
00:10:55,571 --> 00:10:56,906
Really?

195
00:10:57,573 --> 00:10:58,491
Yes!

196
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:01,744
And next year, I'll do even better!

197
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:04,789
And I'll join all the contests!

198
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:09,293
So you'll always be on stage.

199
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:10,920
Oh, no!

200
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:17,385
I might get tired of going up the stage
to put medals on you.

201
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:20,554
But that's what I want.

202
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:26,435
And I also want my classmates to see you.

203
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:28,687
Hmm? Why?

204
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:33,401
So I can say I'm no longer adopted,

205
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:36,070
and I already have a mom.

206
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:41,325
[music fades]

207
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:44,954
[sentimental music playing]

208
00:11:58,050 --> 00:12:02,763
[music fades]

209
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:05,099
Dad, hold on. Please, I beg you.

210
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:06,392
- [groans]
- [sobs]

211
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:07,726
[in English] Dad, please.

212
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:13,107
[suspenseful music playing]

213
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:14,775
- [in English] Wow!
- [gasps]

214
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:18,237
So, this is a family reunion, huh?

215
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,155
[grunts]

216
00:12:19,238 --> 00:12:20,739
Don't come near!

217
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:22,408
You animal! [grunts]

218
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:23,325
[Dmitri, in English] No, Audrey.

219
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:25,286
[Dmitri] Run away!

220
00:12:25,369 --> 00:12:27,037
- [in English] I'm not leaving you here!
- [groans]

221
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:29,206
No. Let us go, Red.

222
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,584
Do you think I'd be scared of your gun?

223
00:12:32,084 --> 00:12:34,044
Do you know how many times
I've had a gun pointed at me?

224
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:35,921
[in English] That's right.

225
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:39,467
I forgot you're evil!

226
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:41,260
[Audrey sobs]

227
00:12:41,343 --> 00:12:43,721
Aside from what you did to our dad…

228
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:48,434
[inhales] You weren't content with that,
you also took my child away!

229
00:12:48,517 --> 00:12:50,102
[tense music playing]

230
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:53,772
You even made me believe Janine
was really my daughter!

231
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:56,317
So, you already know, huh?

232
00:12:57,067 --> 00:12:59,320
You were happy,
even if your child was fake, right?

233
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:01,280
Your life had purpose.

234
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:04,700
[sobs] Where is my real child?!

235
00:13:05,284 --> 00:13:06,994
[Audrey sobs]

236
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:08,245
Who is she?!

237
00:13:09,246 --> 00:13:10,706
- [music swells]
- [clicks tongue]

238
00:13:10,789 --> 00:13:13,501
I'll never tell you, even if you shoot me.

239
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:15,711
[gasping]

240
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:16,795
[growls]

241
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:20,090
[Audrey, in English] You're a monster!

242
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:22,551
[sobbing]

243
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:25,179
[tense music playing]

244
00:13:25,262 --> 00:13:26,514
[in English] A monster?

245
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:28,933
Don't blame me, blame him!

246
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:30,142
Blame him!

247
00:13:30,726 --> 00:13:31,560
Red…

248
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:33,771
Stop it, please.

249
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:35,356
[Red] Stop what? Stop what, huh?!

250
00:13:35,439 --> 00:13:38,275
- [Dmitri] Stop it.
- I put up with this for so long!

251
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:42,738
I'm just starting,
and now you're telling me to stop?!

252
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:46,075
When Mom died, huh!

253
00:13:46,158 --> 00:13:47,910
You think you're the only one
who lost her?!

254
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:49,328
You think you're the only one
who got hurt?!

255
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:52,998
I was hurt too!

256
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:55,459
I lost someone too!

257
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:58,879
But why do you blame me, huh?!

258
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,631
Oh, and you, you!

259
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:02,216
Why didn't you go with her, huh?!

260
00:14:03,342 --> 00:14:04,510
Why did you leave her?!

261
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:08,389
[in English] She was worried about you,
that's why she had the accident!

262
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:12,601
Mom died because of you!

263
00:14:13,185 --> 00:14:16,397
- How dare you blame it on someone else!
- [in English] Oh… Shut up!

264
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:19,733
Whatever you are now, you chose that!

265
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:21,318
Didn't it ever occur to you, huh?!

266
00:14:22,486 --> 00:14:24,029
I struggled to move on, didn't I?!

267
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:25,364
That's why I became like this!

268
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:27,074
[ominous music playing]

269
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:29,869
My whole life,
you all blamed me, didn't you?!

270
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:33,789
Maybe if you just showed me a little love!

271
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:35,040
Just a little!

272
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:37,084
Maybe I wouldn't have grown up
like this, right?!

273
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:38,127
Damn near everything!

274
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:40,254
Everything you wanted me to do, I did!

275
00:14:40,337 --> 00:14:41,630
Even bad things!

276
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,632
I did them to please you!

277
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:46,427
[in English] Yes, you're right!

278
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,970
[in English] I am a monster.

279
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:49,179
[in English] But he created me!

280
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:50,806
[music fades]

281
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:52,808
- [groans, grunts]
- [in English] Dad. Dad!

282
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,059
[Dmitri] Stop it, Red!

283
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:55,895
- [Dmitri] Stop it! Run away!
- [in English] No, Dad!

284
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:57,062
- [in English] Dad!
- [in English] Run away!

285
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:58,105
[in English] No!

286
00:14:58,188 --> 00:15:01,108
- [both grunt, shouting]
- [gunshots]

287
00:15:01,191 --> 00:15:03,736
[in English] Dad!

288
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:06,030
[Dmitri groans]

289
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:09,909
[sobbing]

290
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:11,911
- [wailing]
- [grunts]

291
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:13,287
[groans]

292
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:30,095
[wailing]

293
00:15:31,513 --> 00:15:32,598
Auntie!

294
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,475
- Janine!
- Mommy!

295
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:36,602
[wails]

296
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,062
Auntie, what happened?

297
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:39,355
Gavin… [sobs]

298
00:15:39,438 --> 00:15:41,815
Gavin, Red shot your grandfather!

299
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:43,359
[in English] What? Why?

300
00:15:43,442 --> 00:15:46,862
We need to get out of here
because he wants to kill us too!

301
00:15:47,446 --> 00:15:48,280
Get in here.

302
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:49,406
Ma'am, what happened, ma'am?

303
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:51,659
Run, run away!

304
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:53,911
- You might get dragged into this!
- [Gavin] Please open the gate!

305
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:56,205
[Audrey] My brother is out of his mind!

306
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:58,290
Put on your seat belt, child!

307
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:00,542
Faster, Gavin!

308
00:16:01,168 --> 00:16:03,087
[in English] Go! Go!

309
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:09,510
[music fades]

310
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:12,471
How did we end up like this?

311
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:17,059
[pensive music playing]

312
00:16:17,142 --> 00:16:19,103
Father and son killing each other.

313
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:24,775
[in English] You know, Dad…

314
00:16:26,026 --> 00:16:27,569
I worshipped you.

315
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:32,116
I loved you so much.

316
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:38,247
You know, at one point,
I felt that you loved me too.

317
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:42,751
[Dmitri, in English] Red, you fold it
this way, like this.

318
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,253
[in English] And then, the wings!

319
00:16:44,336 --> 00:16:45,838
Last part, the wings.

320
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:47,006
That's the wings, okay.

321
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:50,300
Like this, those are the wings. Okay.

322
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:52,344
[in English] Okay!

323
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:55,055
[in English] Now, it's ready to fly!

324
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:56,598
What? Let's do it together, huh!

325
00:16:56,682 --> 00:16:58,017
- Yes.
- [in English] Okay.

326
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:01,311
Here it is. Together?

327
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:02,896
You first, Dad!

328
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:06,442
[in English] Oh, okay. Watch.

329
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,694
[pensive music playing]

330
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:11,321
See? Did you see that?

331
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:13,490
It flew well, right? Now it's your turn.

332
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:15,743
- Okay. That's ready now.
- [in English] Okay.

333
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:16,744
[in English] For sure.

334
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:19,705
[in English] One, two, three!

335
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:25,586
[screams, in English] I hate this!

336
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:28,172
I've made so many!

337
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:30,007
[in English] It doesn't fly!

338
00:17:31,925 --> 00:17:34,887
[screams] I always make mistakes!

339
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:37,681
[in English] Hey. Son, relax. Sit down.

340
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:39,349
[in English] It's okay.

341
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:43,062
It's okay. No matter
how many mistakes you make.

342
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:44,772
Just make another one.

343
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:47,900
I don't count how many mistakes you have.

344
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:51,987
It can be 100 or more than 100,
that's fine with me!

345
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:54,615
[in English] It's okay. Okay?

346
00:17:55,199 --> 00:17:58,786
[in English] All you have to do
is make another one.

347
00:17:58,869 --> 00:17:59,787
[in English] Okay?

348
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:01,580
- [in English] Okay?
- [in English] Okay, Dad.

349
00:18:01,663 --> 00:18:03,373
Let's make another one, huh.

350
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,334
[in English] Okay, here.

351
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:08,212
[in English] That's your paper
and this is my paper. Okay.

352
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:10,923
[pensive music playing]

353
00:18:11,548 --> 00:18:14,343
You said you wouldn't count
my mistakes, right?

354
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:16,178
[in English] I remember that.

355
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:24,144
You said, even if reaches 100 or more,

356
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:27,314
you wouldn't count them.

357
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:28,774
[sharp inhale]

358
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:32,152
[sharp inhale]

359
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:34,029
When did you start counting?

360
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,782
[heavy breathing]

361
00:18:36,865 --> 00:18:38,325
I can't remember.

362
00:18:38,408 --> 00:18:39,701
[sobbing]

363
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:41,411
When Mommy died…

364
00:18:41,912 --> 00:18:43,831
[sobs]

365
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:45,958
I didn't feel like I was your son anymore.

366
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:48,919
[sobbing]

367
00:18:49,002 --> 00:18:51,421
It seemed like it was so hard
for you to love me.

368
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:55,759
[sobs] Dad…

369
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:58,137
Did it ever occur to you?

370
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:02,224
I wouldn't have become like this
if you hadn't deprived me of love.

371
00:19:02,307 --> 00:19:03,267
[sobs]

372
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:04,810
[in English] You think I wanted this?

373
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:08,105
[sobbing]

374
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:11,108
You deprived me!

375
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:16,155
- [sobs]
- [heavy breathing]

376
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:27,082
[in English] I'm… I'm sorry, my son.

377
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,292
[gasps]

378
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:31,879
[in English] I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

379
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:35,716
[in English] I'm sorry. [sobs]

380
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,551
[in English] I'm sorry!

381
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:40,554
[in English] I'm sorry, my son.

382
00:19:40,637 --> 00:19:43,098
[in English] I'm sorry, my son.

383
00:19:44,099 --> 00:19:45,392
[in English] It's just not enough.

384
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:47,269
[gunshot]

385
00:19:47,352 --> 00:19:50,397
[epic music playing]

386
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:02,034
[exhales]

387
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:26,934
[music fades]

388
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:44,076
[Atoy] Sorry, Lily.

389
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:47,788
We won't be able to get out anymore.

390
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:52,501
We'll rot here.

391
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:56,672
Why are you saying that?

392
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:01,551
I can't stay here, Atoy.

393
00:21:03,845 --> 00:21:05,889
My child still needs me.

394
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:08,767
I need to live.

395
00:21:10,143 --> 00:21:11,937
I thought you were going to save me.

396
00:21:14,231 --> 00:21:15,274
Save you?

397
00:21:19,903 --> 00:21:21,947
Why would I save you?

398
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:27,911
Why, huh?

399
00:21:29,579 --> 00:21:31,039
Are you a good person?

400
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:36,920
You're in cahoots with them, aren't you?

401
00:21:38,714 --> 00:21:40,215
You work for them.

402
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:44,761
You knew that the information you have
is very important to national security.

403
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,972
[pensive music playing]

404
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:50,142
You're involved in this, right?

405
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:52,519
You knew they were training.

406
00:21:52,602 --> 00:21:53,895
What's their purpose?

407
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:55,981
They're terrorists.

408
00:21:56,064 --> 00:21:59,568
They won't do anything
but kill millions of Filipinos.

409
00:22:00,110 --> 00:22:02,654
And now, you want me to save you? [huffs]

410
00:22:08,076 --> 00:22:09,745
I regret it now, Atoy.

411
00:22:09,828 --> 00:22:12,456
I just wanted to work for my child.

412
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:15,083
And to extend the lives of my parents too.

413
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:18,503
I'm the only one they rely on.

414
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:20,547
[scoffs]

415
00:22:22,132 --> 00:22:24,509
It's too late for regrets.

416
00:22:28,472 --> 00:22:30,140
We'll rot here.

417
00:22:31,016 --> 00:22:32,225
You're all the same.

418
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:37,564
[Lily sighs]

419
00:22:37,647 --> 00:22:38,648
Atoy.

420
00:22:41,359 --> 00:22:47,824
Everyone makes wrong decisions
that can be corrected.

421
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:51,578
I can't blame you

422
00:22:52,245 --> 00:22:54,748
if you don't want to save me
because of my job.

423
00:22:56,124 --> 00:22:58,335
Just think, I also have a family.

424
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:01,379
Think of the people who love you.

425
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:05,509
I don't believe you don't have a family.

426
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:09,763
I know you only said that to Samir
so no one else would get dragged in.

427
00:23:11,306 --> 00:23:12,682
[melodramatic music playing]

428
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:15,268
Do you know that he won't file
a case against you

429
00:23:15,352 --> 00:23:16,853
because he's thinking about Janine and me?

430
00:23:18,396 --> 00:23:19,439
We are a family.

431
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:21,399
You, me, Janine.

432
00:23:21,483 --> 00:23:22,984
We are a family!

433
00:23:23,068 --> 00:23:24,569
That's what matters most.

434
00:23:24,653 --> 00:23:26,113
We-- We are a family!

435
00:23:26,196 --> 00:23:30,617
But how can I tell our child
that you almost killed her grandfather?!

436
00:23:31,576 --> 00:23:33,036
Janine, my child?

437
00:23:36,081 --> 00:23:38,208
Did Dad hurt Grandpa?

438
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:41,670
- [Janine] Huh?
- [Audrey] Child.

439
00:23:45,465 --> 00:23:46,758
- [Audrey] Let's go, child.
- [Atoy] Child, no.

440
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:47,968
- [Audrey, in English] Please.
- Janine.

441
00:23:49,136 --> 00:23:49,970
[music swells]

442
00:23:50,554 --> 00:23:52,347
[Atoy] <i>I treated you like family!</i>

443
00:23:52,430 --> 00:23:54,432
I've long wanted to tell you everything,

444
00:23:54,516 --> 00:23:59,271
but Delfin told me to keep it from you.

445
00:23:59,354 --> 00:24:00,647
[Atoy] What secret? Don't-- Don't--

446
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:04,109
Don't use Dad to justify
what you did, Godmother!

447
00:24:04,192 --> 00:24:07,070
Forgive me, forgive me.

448
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:10,198
Blame me, not Karla.

449
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:12,534
I just didn't want to ruin what we had.

450
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:14,536
I didn't want to hurt you, Atoy.

451
00:24:14,619 --> 00:24:16,746
Atoy, forgive me.

452
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:17,747
[Atoy] You're unbelievable.

453
00:24:17,831 --> 00:24:19,249
Unbelievable!

454
00:24:19,332 --> 00:24:20,959
[Cita] Atoy. [sobbing]

455
00:24:23,628 --> 00:24:24,921
- I don't need you.
- [Cita] Atoy.

456
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:26,256
[sobbing]

457
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:28,216
[mouthing] You too.

458
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:34,264
[Ibyang] <i>Thank you, Tatoy.</i>

459
00:24:34,347 --> 00:24:36,766
<i>If not for you…</i> [sobs]

460
00:24:36,850 --> 00:24:40,437
<i>I wouldn't have a family.</i>

461
00:24:41,021 --> 00:24:43,857
<i>No one can replace you</i>

462
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:47,444
<i>because I love you.</i>

463
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:53,241
[Atoy] <i>Because of you,</i>
<i>I got to know myself better.</i>

464
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:55,410
<i>That's why I love you so much, Ibyang.</i>

465
00:24:55,493 --> 00:24:57,537
[Ibyang sobbing]

466
00:24:57,621 --> 00:24:58,997
[Atoy] <i>I'll miss you.</i>

467
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:04,044
[epic music playing]

468
00:25:04,127 --> 00:25:05,754
What I said is true.

469
00:25:05,837 --> 00:25:06,755
[sharp inhale]

470
00:25:07,797 --> 00:25:09,758
I have no family anymore.

471
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:13,720
No one cares about me now.

472
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:17,849
My life has no meaning anymore.

473
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:22,312
[music swells]

474
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:35,492
[henchman] Here.

475
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:37,452
Your food!

476
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:41,665
Eat it yourself.

477
00:25:41,748 --> 00:25:44,834
[pensive music playing]

478
00:25:44,918 --> 00:25:45,877
[grunts]

479
00:25:45,961 --> 00:25:48,004
[groans]

480
00:25:48,713 --> 00:25:49,547
What?

481
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:51,841
Is that all you can do, huh?!

482
00:25:51,925 --> 00:25:53,927
Go ahead! Kick me again!

483
00:25:54,010 --> 00:25:55,053
You're nothing!

484
00:25:55,136 --> 00:25:57,472
Eat that! Kick me again if you want!

485
00:25:57,555 --> 00:25:59,432
Do whatever you want! Go on!

486
00:25:59,516 --> 00:26:01,017
- [henchman] Ah, is that so?
- Go on!

487
00:26:01,101 --> 00:26:02,727
[grunts and groans] Go on!

488
00:26:03,728 --> 00:26:05,272
[Lily] Stop it!

489
00:26:08,525 --> 00:26:11,278
What? What, are you done?!

490
00:26:11,361 --> 00:26:12,195
Go on!

491
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:15,282
Kill me now,
so I can join my mother and father!

492
00:26:15,365 --> 00:26:16,908
[Lily] Atoy!

493
00:26:16,992 --> 00:26:17,993
[groans]

494
00:26:18,994 --> 00:26:20,287
Don't cause any more trouble.

495
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:21,997
Why are you doing this to yourself?

496
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,581
Have mercy.

497
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:27,585
[music fades]

498
00:26:27,669 --> 00:26:29,296
[exhales]

499
00:26:29,379 --> 00:26:33,466
You know, I feel you're a good person
because you risked your life to…

500
00:26:33,550 --> 00:26:34,926
to save me.

501
00:26:35,427 --> 00:26:36,928
[pensive music playing]

502
00:26:37,012 --> 00:26:38,305
That was just work.

503
00:26:39,931 --> 00:26:42,600
I could die here so it would all be over.

504
00:26:42,684 --> 00:26:44,394
Don't say that.

505
00:26:44,477 --> 00:26:46,438
You shouldn't give up.

506
00:26:47,355 --> 00:26:49,858
Because you're still important
to other people.

507
00:26:49,941 --> 00:26:52,193
Even if you say you don't have a family.

508
00:26:53,653 --> 00:26:57,198
Surely, you left a mark
on at least one person.

509
00:27:01,369 --> 00:27:03,079
"Tatoy, Tatoy,

510
00:27:03,663 --> 00:27:05,915
thank you for your love.

511
00:27:05,999 --> 00:27:09,753
Every day, I always feel it.

512
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:14,424
Because of you, my life is so happy."

513
00:27:15,133 --> 00:27:16,718
Come here. Thank you.

514
00:27:17,302 --> 00:27:18,845
- [melodramatic music playing]
- [Ibyang] Mmm.

515
00:27:22,557 --> 00:27:23,558
[soft moan]

516
00:27:52,837 --> 00:27:55,673
Audrey escaped, and that child

517
00:27:55,757 --> 00:27:57,842
is the only way to bring Audrey back here.
She won't speak.

518
00:27:57,926 --> 00:27:59,677
Just think about what Atoy would do

519
00:27:59,761 --> 00:28:02,222
if he found out that Ibyang
is really his true child.

520
00:28:02,305 --> 00:28:04,391
Ibyang is Atoy's child?

521
00:28:04,474 --> 00:28:05,392
What did you hear?

522
00:28:05,475 --> 00:28:06,893
I'll tell Atoy everything.

523
00:28:06,976 --> 00:28:07,894
UP NEXT

524
00:28:07,977 --> 00:28:09,854
- [in English] Not so fast.
- [shrieks]

525
00:28:09,938 --> 00:28:11,815
- Is Uno there?
- He's inside. Why?

526
00:28:11,898 --> 00:28:12,941
I think he's a spy.

527
00:28:13,024 --> 00:28:14,818
[Karla] <i>Maybe he's working</i>
<i>for Red Regalia.</i>

528
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:16,277
- Caught you!
- [Karla] I knew it.

529
00:28:16,361 --> 00:28:18,154
- My suspicion was right!
- [grunts]

530
00:28:18,238 --> 00:28:19,239
[grunts and groans]

531
00:28:19,322 --> 00:28:21,908
Boss, what if Audrey
went to another police station?

532
00:28:22,492 --> 00:28:23,827
There's only one person they'll go to.

533
00:28:23,910 --> 00:28:26,413
[Charmi] <i>Don't do anything bad.</i>

534
00:28:28,706 --> 00:28:31,793
[in English] Don't tell me
that you don't know them.

535
00:28:31,876 --> 00:28:34,170
If I find out you hurt them…

536
00:28:35,088 --> 00:28:40,510
I'll stitch you to the wall,
and feed you to animals like you.

537
00:28:40,593 --> 00:28:41,803
[in English] Good luck with that.

538
00:28:42,804 --> 00:28:44,931
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

539
00:28:45,014 --> 00:28:47,892
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

540
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:50,061
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

541
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:51,730
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
